Thanks for the revised BOM and the Herholdt's quote. The client has come back: R355k is too much against the 36-month saving, and they want an itemised, more modest option. I have costed your revision and it only takes about R5k off - the 25 outdoor APs (R1,885 each) cost more than the 28 indoor ones (R1,025) they replace, so the saving from fewer radios and switches disappears. Before I re-quote I need the following from you, today if possible:

COSTS (ex VAT, from actual stock or supplier quotes - no estimates)
1. 6m mast with plinth, installed - our cost from stock.
2. Bare outdoor cabinet (MPPT, battery and inverter now come from the Herholdt's kit).
3. 4U wall boxes x4.
4. Unmanaged 6-port PoE switches x2.
5. Extended warranties (4500L x2, 4525L x25) - price, and whether you think we need them, or offer them as an option. Also the TP-Link indoor/outdoor AP prices from Pinnacle if you have them.

ENGINEERING (from the survey, please be straight about the risk)
A. Is 6m enough for clear LOS to the staff village (2.3-3 km) AND for Vodacom from Olifants Nek? If 9m is the safe answer, say so - I would rather pay for the height than lose the link.
B. Which buildings genuinely need an OUTDOOR AP? My assumption is the villa, main lodge and boma (say 4); indoor ceiling APs everywhere else. Confirm or correct.
C. The 10 staff houses at 3 km: can they run on 3 subscriber radios with LAN cable between clustered houses instead of 10 radios? If yes, roughly what cable length and trenching are we talking about?

Also: cabling. The quote carries 40m total at R12/m. With 25 sites that is not right - I am moving it to 40m per site. If you have real run lengths from the survey, send them.

